.Dd September 29, 2026
.Dt SP 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm sp
.Nd use hardware-protected personal and shared CloudKit vaults
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar options
.Sh DESCRIPTION
2ndPass v7 generates independent, non-exportable device agreement and signing
keys in Secure Enclave.
Personal vaults are the one-member case of shared vaults.
Same-account enrollment is automatic when an unlocked owner app processes the
exchange.
Cross-account sharing requires independent verification and explicit owner
approval.
The application, AutoFill and CLI share device-local encrypted checkpoints and
device-only Keychain representations.
There is no software-key fallback, old-format reader, migration or portable
recovery private key.
.Pp
Plaintext passwords and temporary per-item keys reach application memory.
Commands receiving a password receive plaintext.
Removing access protects later changes, but cannot erase copied secrets or old
backups.
.Sh COMMANDS
Use
.Nm command --help
for complete arguments.
Secret commands are read, write, list, delete, run, inject and item.
Values are supplied by hidden prompt or stdin, never positional password
arguments.
References use sp://vault/item/[section/]field.
.Pp
Device request creates a public enrollment document.
Vault init inherits the account's configured offline recovery authority.
.Pp
Vault invite, accept and approve exchange public documents, independently
compared fingerprints/checkpoints and (for other accounts) a private iCloud
share URL.
An iCloud invitation alone cannot decrypt the vault.
Members, remove-member, remove-device, role and reconcile-share manage access.
.Pp
Vault list includes trusted roots and untrusted iCloud enrollment hints.
Rename changes references.
Sync verifies signed descendants and reconciles uncertain commits without
replaying edits.
Export writes an encrypted checkpoint; import requires independent checkpoint
evidence and an already enrolled device.
.Pp
Vault recovery generate exports an offline copy; activate requires re-import
and the displayed public fingerprint. Status reports account-wide coverage.
Open provides same-account read-only recovery; --complete rotates access.
Resume continues incomplete lifecycle changes; revoke removes the offline key.
Keep both offline copies until replacement finishes. This does not restore
Apple Account access or missing cloud data.
.Pp
Vault delete requires --vault UUID --confirm UUID.
It deletes the cloud zone; existing local ciphertext and exported backups
remain.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Fl -vault Ar NAME-OR-UUID
constrains selection.
Management requires an explicit selection when multiple vaults are registered.
.Pp
.Fl -offline
uses a previously verified checkpoint read-only.
Remote revocation and unobserved account changes cannot be detected offline.
.Pp
.Fl -state-directory Ar PATH
or MOP_STATE_DIRECTORY overrides device-local state.
Never synchronize it.
.Sh SECURITY
Operational access requires a provisioned signed application, matching
Keychain access group/CloudKit environment, Secure Enclave and local
authentication.
Every fill starts fresh authorization.
GUI contexts last until lock/expiry; hardware handles and individual secret
keys are released after operations.
.Pp
Conflicting edits fail.
Submitted operations may finish after cancellation; journals and conditional
version barriers determine their outcome.
Do not blindly repeat an uncertain mutation.
No existing old-format data is deleted.
.Pp
Read emits plaintext to stdout or an output file.
Inject writes literal plaintext to stdout or a generated file, without
format-specific escaping.
Run passes resolved secrets in the child environment.
That child, its dependencies and inheriting descendants become trusted with
those secrets.
Environment variables may be exposed by the program, diagnostics or privileged
host software.
Default masking filters exact secret bytes in captured stdout/stderr only; it
cannot constrain transformed output, files or network disclosure.
.Pp
Same-account enrollment composes Apple's account security, code signing,
provisioning and CloudKit entitlements with private per-user storage and a
signed 2ndPass membership grant.
Account credentials alone do not permit arbitrary container writes.
An attacker able to operate an authorized client in that user's iCloud context
may obtain membership if an unlocked owner processes the exchange.
.Pp
Secure Enclave resists extraction and portability of device private keys, not
malicious use on an unlocked endpoint.
Offline recovery requires the recovery copy, access to the same Apple Account,
and accessible cloud ciphertext. The copy cannot recover Apple Account access.
Anyone with the private recovery secret and copied ciphertext can decrypt it.
.Pp
2ndPass is not independently audited.
Signed revisions detect unauthorized changes and rollback relative to intact
trusted local state, not withheld newer updates or absolute freshness.
Physical-device acceptance remains a release gate.
.Pp
Cross-account vault sharing is not yet implemented as a supported feature.
Preliminary code would share the enrollment mailbox's zone.
Account-private mailbox isolation must be addressed when implementing sharing.
This is a design detail, not a current product vulnerability;
see docs/SECURITY.md.
.Sh SEE ALSO
The project README, docs/SECURITY.md and docs/VAULT-NEXT-VALIDATION.md
describe workflows, precise platform boundaries and remaining physical-device
checks.
.Sh ICLOUD DEVICE ENROLLMENT
Use vault enrollment request on the new device, inbox on an existing owner,
status and confirm --code MATCHING_CODE on the new device, then approve
--request-id UUID --code MATCHING_CODE on the owner after comparing both
displays.
A final status finishes enrollment.
The CLI commands provide a manual diagnostic exchange.
The app performs same-account enrollment automatically without required human
code comparison or approval; a concurrent unlocked owner app may grant a
pending request.
Decline rejects a request.
Requests expire after one day.
This flow is for the same Apple Account; sharing with another account remains
separate.
.Pp
Use enrollment restart on the new device to replace a stuck request without
replacing its hardware keys.
Enrollment cancel stops the pending request.
Neither command deletes vault contents or revokes access already granted.
The app displays request status, expiry and the last successful iCloud check.
.Sh DEVICE REMOVAL
.Sy sp vault devices
lists own-account devices across enrolled personal vaults.
.Sy sp vault devices --remove UUID
revokes a device across those vaults.
The last owner device cannot be removed.
The removed device clears its local access after observing the signed
revocation.
.Sy sp vault enrollment reconnect
explicitly permits fresh-key enrollment after removal; follow it with
.Sy sp vault enrollment request --vault UUID
while another owner device is unlocked.

.Sh SUBSCRIPTION STATUS
.Nm subscription status
.Op Fl Fl json
.Op Fl Fl offline
.Pp
Report shared Pro subscription evidence without restricting commands.
Operational commands emit a concise status on stderr; stdout and exit codes
retain their existing meanings. Offline checks use previously verified evidence
through its expiration or billing-grace deadline, without an extension.
Development CloudKit builds are explicitly exempt.
